---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Invitations">
  <h1>Invitations</h1>
  <p>Admins can invite users without exposing self-serve signup. The invitation flow is implemented end-to-end: an admin calls <code>InviteUser</code>, the invitee uses the returned token to call <code>AcceptInvitation</code>, and the result is a fully active user with a fresh session.</p>

  <h2>Two modes</h2>
  <p>Set <code>create_immediately</code> on <code>InviteUserRequest</code>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>false</strong> &mdash; creates a pending User (<code>status=invited</code>) and returns a one-time <code>invitation_token</code> + <code>setup_url</code>. The user finishes signup via <code>AcceptInvitation</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>true</strong> &mdash; creates a fully active User and returns a <code>temporary_password</code> the admin hands off. Useful for offline onboarding.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Invite (deferred)</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/InviteUser \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "role": "member",
    "recovery_email": "newperson-backup@example.com",
    "create_immediately": false
  }'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": {
    "id": "user_01HX...",
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "status": "USER_STATUS_INVITED",
    "role": "member"
  },
  "invitationToken": "inv_...",
  "setupUrl": "https://app.example.com/accept-invite?token=inv_..."
}</code></pre>
  <p>The invitee opens <code>setup_url</code>, picks a password, and the frontend calls:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/AcceptInvitation \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "invitation_token": "inv_...",
    "password": "Their5tronger#Pass",
    "name": "New Person"
  }'
# &rarr; { user (now status=active), accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn }</code></pre>
  <p><code>AcceptInvitation</code> is auth-exempt, so it works with no prior session. The user is logged in immediately on success.</p>

  <h2>Invite (immediate)</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">curl -s -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/InviteUser \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_ACCESS" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "newperson@example.com",
    "name": "New Person",
    "role": "member",
    "create_immediately": true
  }'</code></pre>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-json">{
  "user": { "id": "user_01HX...", "status": "USER_STATUS_ACTIVE" },
  "temporaryPassword": "Tmp-q9wK7s5N..."
}</code></pre>
  <p>The temporary password is shown to the admin <em>once</em>. Hand it to the user out-of-band; they should change it on first login via <code>ChangePassword</code>.</p>

  <Callout type="warning" title="Admin role required">
    All invitation RPCs (<code>InviteUser</code>, <code>DeactivateUser</code>, <code>ReactivateUser</code>, <code>ResetUserPassword</code>, <code>SetUserQuota</code>) require the calling JWT to have <code>role=admin</code>. The <code>AdminService.requireAdmin</code> helper enforces this; non-admin callers get <code>permission_denied</code> with no effect on the target.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Audit events</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>user_invited</code> &mdash; emitted on every <code>InviteUser</code> call. Includes target user ID, role, and whether the immediate-create path was used.</li>
    <li><code>login_success</code> &mdash; emitted when the invitee completes <code>AcceptInvitation</code>, with <code>method=invitation</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Token characteristics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Generated as a random opaque string by the server.</li>
    <li>Single-use &mdash; consumed atomically by <code>AcceptInvitation</code>.</li>
    <li>Stored hashed alongside the User node so the raw token can't be recovered server-side.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
